{"entity": "Wuhan P&S Information Technology Co., Ltd.", "type": "organization", "description": "Wuhan P&S Information Technology Co., Ltd. (武汉力源信息技术股份有限公司, also referred to as 力源信息 or 力源有限, and formerly known as Wuhan P&S Information Technology Service Co., Ltd./力源服务) is a Chinese joint-stock company headquartered in Wuhan, Hubei. Established on August 9, 2001, with registered capital of RMB 50 million and legal representative Zhao Mark, it was converted into a joint-stock company on December 8, 2009 through the overall conversion of Liyuan Limited, inheriting all assets, debts, and personnel while operating independently in assets, business, personnel, finance, and organization. Its address is Hongshan Venture Building, 424 Luoyu Road, Hongshan District, Wuhan. The company is issuing shares for the first time and applying for listing on the ChiNext market, proposing to publicly issue 16.7 million A shares via a prospectus (招股意向书). Major shareholders holding over 5% include Mark Zhao, Rongbing Investment, Tingyin Investment, Lianzhong Juyuan, Wuhan Borun, and Shanghai Borun, with equity also held by Shanghai Borun and Wuhan Borun.\n\nThe company is a well-known IC catalog distributor in China, mainly engaged in the promotion, sale, and application services of semiconductor integrated circuits (ICs) and other electronic components, serving as an important link between upstream manufacturers and downstream users in the IC industry chain. Positioned as a technology-service-oriented IC catalog distributor, it combines passive \"store-style\" selling with proactive consultative marketing, offering large in-stock inventory, product catalogs, online inquiry/ordering/payment, and technical support including information materials, product selection, and reference solutions. It distributes products from 18 well-known domestic and international semiconductor manufacturers, with over 10 product categories and more than 15,000 in-stock product models covering microcontrollers, 