{"entity": "IC", "type": "artifact", "description": "An integrated circuit (IC) is a micro electronic device that integrates transistors, diodes, resistors, capacitors, inductors, and wiring on a semiconductor wafer, packaged into a micro structure capable of required circuit functions. ICs serve as the foundational components of electronic products and are considered high-technology building blocks of final products, forming the core of modern industry. They are characterized as a commodity with four key features: few original manufacturers with concentrated market share, numerous product models, wide industry usage, and high technical requirements. As technology-intensive products, IC design and manufacturing are concentrated among a small number of original manufacturers, with global production similarly concentrated in a few companies, while China stands as the largest consumer market. In 2008, China's IC market demand reached 597.33 billion yuan, with small and medium electronic industrial enterprises generating demand for over 100,000 types of ICs.\n\nThe IC industry is a fundamental sector of a modern nation's national economy. Its industry chain typically consists of IC manufacturing, IC sales, and electronic product design and manufacturing. ICs are the main focus of sales and customer demand for companies such as 力源信息 (Liyuan Information), whose technical services are based on further development and application of IC functions, mastering and extending IC electronic component functions beyond the original manufacturer's settings. Small-batch IC products demanded by the R&D market are distributed by companies including Digi-Key and P&S Information."}
