{"entity": "Wuhan P&S Information Technology Co., Ltd.", "type": "organization", "description": "Wuhan P&S Information Technology Co., Ltd. (武汉力源信息技术股份有限公司, also referred to as 力源信息 or 力源有限, and formerly known as Wuhan P&S Information Technology Service Co., Ltd./力源服务) is a Chinese joint-stock company headquartered in Wuhan, Hubei. Established on August 9, 2001, with registered capital of RMB 50 million and legal representative Zhao Mark, it was converted into a joint-stock company on December 8, 2009 through the overall conversion of Liyuan Limited, inheriting all assets, debts, and personnel while operating independently in assets, business, personnel, finance, and organization. Its address is Hongshan Venture Building, 424 Luoyu Road, Hongshan District, Wuhan. The company is issuing shares for the first time and applying for listing on the ChiNext market, proposing to publicly issue 16.7 million A shares via a prospectus (招股意向书). Major shareholders holding over 5% include Mark Zhao, Rongbing Investment, Tingyin Investment, Lianzhong Juyuan, Wuhan Borun, and Shanghai Borun, with equity also held by Shanghai Borun and Wuhan Borun.\n\nThe company is a well-known IC catalog distributor in China, mainly engaged in the promotion, sale, and application services of semiconductor integrated circuits (ICs) and other electronic components, serving as an important link between upstream manufacturers and downstream users in the IC industry chain. Positioned as a technology-service-oriented IC catalog distributor, it combines passive \"store-style\" selling with proactive consultative marketing, offering large in-stock inventory, product catalogs, online inquiry/ordering/payment, and technical support including information materials, product selection, and reference solutions. It distributes products from 18 well-known domestic and international semiconductor manufacturers, with over 10 product categories and more than 15,000 in-stock product models covering microcontrollers, system management devices, interface devices, and data conversion, and serves over 100,000 registered customers and more than 7,400 active trading customers. Its target market focuses on industrial control applications and the IC retail market. It was recognized as a \"High-Tech Enterprise\" in 2008, and has been repeatedly selected as a \"Most Satisfied IC Distributor by Readers\" in International Electronic Business Times since 2003.\n\nThe company introduced the foreign IC catalog sales model to China, adapting it to local conditions. It operates a telephone/network sales center in Wuhan, six sales offices nationwide, and 26 cooperative retail outlets, processing over 30,000 transactions and 100,000 orders annually, with sales methods including telephone/network sales, channel sales, sales office sales, and key account sales, as well as catalog, in-stock, and reference design solutions. It purchases IC products from original manufacturers and distributors, including through Liyuan Trading and Hong Kong Liyuan (Hong Kong P&S), and manages commodities in a database, using commercial insurance to protect inventory cost value, warehouse management systems, and anti-static warehouses, while handling quality disputes and returns/exchanges. Its business scope covers development, research, production, sales, and technical services of electronic products, electronic components, information technology, and related complete product solutions. It has applied reference designs for finger-clip oximeters, multi-parameter medical monitors, bank/tax-control POS machines, in-vehicle GPS, dome cameras, KVM, Cat-5 long-line differential image transmission, HDMI extenders/switchers, low-power switching power supplies, miner's lamps, and VGA splitters, and has applied for five utility model patents with two more pending. It owns trademarks, patents, patent applications, software copyrights, and other intangible assets, and leases office space.\n\nThe company reported employee growth from 82 at the end of 2007 to 118 by June 30, 2010, with staff in Wuhan, Beijing, Shenzhen, Chengdu, and Shanghai, and established a Shanghai branch in July 2009. Its prospectus describes semiconductor device sales revenue, regional distribution, and sales models from 2007 to the first half of 2010, along with industry characteristics such as technical strength, distribution models, and regional patterns. The company plans to expand supplier scale, product variety, customer base, and sales revenue through fundraising projects."}
