{"entity": "陈爱民", "type": "person", "description": "陈爱民 is a Chinese businessman and key figure in the founding, development, and management of Wuhan Xingtu Xinke Electronics Co., Ltd. (武汉兴图新科电子股份有限公司) and its predecessor, Wuhan Xingtu Xinke Electronics Co., Ltd. (武汉兴图新科电子有限公司). On June 17, 2004, he co-founded the predecessor company with 程家明. At its establishment, he contributed office computers and an Midea central air conditioner as capital, along with 62,300 yuan in cash and 87,700 yuan in kind, initially holding a stake that later converted to 8.50%. He is a natural person shareholder and promoter of both the predecessor and the current company. Over time his direct stake was diluted; after the January 2017 capital change he held 2,325,600 shares (4.63%), and subsequently 2,325,600 shares representing 4.45%, then 4.21% before the company's issuance. In addition, he indirectly holds 1,520,000 shares (2.75%) and holds a 14.29% stake in Xingtu Investment (兴图投资), corresponding to a capital contribution of 1.72 million yuan.\n\n陈爱民 is also a director and deputy general manager of Wuhan Xingtu Xinke Electronics Co., Ltd., a position he has held continuously over the past two years. He was elected director of the company's third board of directors on June 21, 2017, and appointed deputy general manager on the same date. He concurrently serves as the legal representative of Beijing Huachuang Xingtu Electronic Technology Co., Ltd. (北京华创兴图电子科技有限公司), and as executive director and manager (later general manager) of Xing Tu Tian Jian (兴图天建) and Huachuang Xingtu (华创兴图). He is also the legal representative or responsible person of Xingtu Tianjian and its Wuhan branch. In 2018, his total remuneration from the company was 446,200 yuan, received as a full-time salary, reflecting his full-time role in management. He is the cousin of 程家明 and the spouse of 关红梅."}
