{"entity": "Wuhan Xingtu Xinke Electronics Co., Ltd.", "type": "organization", "description": "Wuhan Xingtu Xinke Electronics Co., Ltd. is a Chinese joint-stock company that is pursuing an initial public offering (IPO) on the Science and Technology Innovation Board of the Shanghai Stock Exchange, as evidenced by its issuance of an A-share prospectus (招股意向书). The prospectus covers issuance overview, risk factors, basic company information, business and technology, corporate governance, and financial data, along with planned fundraising projects, listing standards, share type, number of shares, and pricing. The company's registered capital increased to 55.20 million yuan in August 2018. Before the issuance, its shareholder equity structure and related-party relationships were disclosed, with no state-owned, foreign, or strategic investor shares. Chen Shengliang, Cheng Jiezhen, and Ren Qing have held various positions, and the company has a supervisory board with three members. The issuer bears issuance expenses including sponsor fees, underwriting fees, audit and capital verification fees, lawyer fees, information disclosure fees, and issuance handling fees, and has signed labor contracts and confidentiality agreements with directors, supervisors, senior management, and core technical personnel.\n\nThe company independently develops audio-video integrated service platforms and video command and control systems, based on network communication, with a focus on technological and product innovation in the audio-video field. Its core technologies include audio-video middleware, network adaptation in complex environments, and low-latency codec. Main products include video command and control systems (such as the Networked Video Command System and Display Control System) and video early-warning control systems, as well as codecs, servers, and terminal equipment. It designs and produces embedded hardware products such as codecs, servers, and terminal equipment, with self-deve